{
  "$comment": [
    "USPA's official kilogram-to-pound conversion chart, transcribed from the PDF cited",
    "in `chart`.",
    "",
    "This file is the toolkit's only copy of these numbers. Every surface that shows a",
    "USPA conversion -- the direct lookup, the barbell milestones, the full chart, the",
    "text a lifter copies -- reads the artifact published from here. A second copy",
    "anywhere would be a second chart that agrees until the day USPA revises one of",
    "them.",
    "",
    "The rows are transcribed, never generated. That distinction is the whole point of",
    "the file: the chart is what the federation publishes, and a table this project",
    "calculated would be a table this project could be wrong about on its own. It",
    "happens that every row here is reproducible from the factor printed on the chart",
    "itself -- see `chart.statedFactor` -- and the ingestion adapter checks that, but a",
    "check is not a source. If a future revision prints a row the factor does not",
    "reproduce, the row wins and the check reports it.",
    "",
    "HOW THIS WAS VERIFIED, 2026-08-01",
    "",
    "Four passes, three of them independent of each other:",
    "",
    "  1. The PDF's text layer read row-major (`pdftotext -layout`, which reconstructs",
    "     the printed five-column grid) and column-major (plain `pdftotext`, which",
    "     follows the content stream down one column at a time). Different traversals,",
    "     different intermediate text, 180 pairs, no disagreement.",
    "  2. The page rendered to an image and read against this file by eye. This is the",
    "     pass that would catch a text layer that does not say what the page shows.",
    "  3. Every row checked against the factor the chart prints. All 180 reproduce.",
    "  4. Structure: 25 kg to 472.5 kg, uniform 2.5 kg increment, no duplicate and no",
    "     missing kilogram value in the published range.",
    "",
    "WHAT IS NOT HERE",
    "",
    "There is no pounds-to-kilograms chart, because USPA does not publish one. A pound",
    "value is therefore looked up against the pound column of these same rows, which is",
    "why the tool answers a pound question with the two chart rows around it rather than",
    "with a kilogram figure of its own invention.",
    "",
    "The PDF is not committed. It carries the federation's logo, and nothing here needs",
    "it: `chart.sha256` pins the exact bytes this transcription was taken from, and",
    "`check:upstream` re-downloads and re-digests them on a schedule, so a revision",
    "announces itself without the document being redistributed."
  ],
